                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>On September 4 the Department of State reiterated to the Embassy in Borne its
                    policy of supporting impartially all moderate political elements in Italy. It
                    stated that the United States would welcome support for participation in the
                    Italian Government of the greatest possible number of moderate left, center and
                    right groups prepared to work together in harmony, without regard to narrow
                    party differences, for the best interests of the Italian people. The Department
                    further stated: “Obviously, we shall not support extremists, but it must be
                    clear also that we cannot support those who, while not themselves of extreme
                    left or right, make common cause with extremists to detriment of general
                    welfare.” (Telegram 1593 to Borne, September 4, 1947:865.00/8–2847)</p>
            </div>
